rs, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +8.6pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -19% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 41%.","The business throws off $281M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.16\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 30% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 117% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.1722698664290034},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $17.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Unveiling Globale Online (GLBE) Q3 Outlook: Wall Street Estimates for Key Metrics","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029388/unveiling-globale-online-glbe-q3-outlook-wall-street-estimates-for-key-metrics?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm_preview-3029388","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575709.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance","product"]},{"title":"Global-E Online's Q3 Earnings Coming Up: Factors to Watch for GLBE","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029359/global-e-online-s-q3-earnings-coming-up-factors-to-watch-for-glbe?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cearnings_preview-3029359","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575160.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(GLBE) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/20/GLBE_Volatility_Zones_as_Tactical_Triggers_111126014201_1794422521.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794422521.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Glob